  "alt": "Five failure modes that recur in production agent incidents. Context exhaustion: tool results pile up until the context window is full and the next call is rejected. Schema drift: the model calls a tool with parameters from an older schema version. Partial failure: some parallel tool calls succeed and some fail. Ambiguous timeout: a request times out after the server may already have processed it, so a retry can execute it twice. Observability gaps: without structured logs of tool calls there is no record of what the agent tried.",
  "caption": "Each mode has its own fix: a hard cap on tool history, versioned schemas, per-call tracking, idempotency keys, and a log line for every tool call.",
  "embed": "<figure class=\"np-figure\">\n  <a class=\"np-figure-zoom\" href=\"/static/images/diagrams/agent-error-handling/error-taxonomy.svg\"><picture><source media=\"(max-width: 712px)\" srcset=\"/static/images/diagrams/agent-error-handling/error-taxonomy.narrow.svg\" width=\"288\" height=\"704\"><img class=\"np-has-narrow\" src=\"/static/images/diagrams/agent-error-handling/error-taxonomy.svg\" width=\"720\" height=\"264\" alt=\"Five failure modes that recur in production agent incidents. Context exhaustion: tool results pile up until the context window is full and the next call is rejected. Schema drift: the model calls a tool with parameters from an older schema version. Partial failure: some parallel tool calls succeed and some fail. Ambiguous timeout: a request times out after the server may already have processed it, so a retry can execute it twice. Observability gaps: without structured logs of tool calls there is no record of what the agent tried.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></picture></a>\n  <figcaption>Each mode has its own fix: a hard cap on tool history, versioned schemas, per-call tracking, idempotency keys, and a log line for every tool call.</figcaption>\n</figure>"
}
